Author: Gabe Castro <gabe@techworx.dev>
Date:   Sat Aug 8 10:38:14 2026 +0100

    fix(format): exclude pre-release versions from caret range coverage

    caret_covers(cur, new) was returning true when `new` had the same major
    version as `cur` but carried a pre-release suffix (e.g., 1.9.0-alpha.1).
    This meant that ^1.2.3 would incorrectly satisfy 1.9.0-alpha.1, which
    violates the SemVer/Cargo/npm convention that caret ranges cover only
    stable releases within the permitted major/minor bounds.

    Fix: add an early-return for new.is_prerelease() after the < check so
    that any pre-release candidate is unconditionally excluded from coverage.
    Stable versions within the same major continue to be covered as before.

    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NSixbn1hHH7WLXGqzF3GCz

